<title>USA: Ultralife Q3 shr loss $0.34 vs loss $0.01.</title>
<headline>Ultralife Q3 shr loss $0.34 vs loss $0.01.</headline>
<dateline>NEWARK, N.Y. 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>						     March 31,</p>
<p>						1997	    1996</p>
<p>Total revenue		     $  4,381,185   $  4,177,241</p>
<p>Operating (Loss)		    (2,241,779)	(938,300)</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss)		   (2,700,441)	(121,063)</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss) Per Share		(0.34)	   (0.01)</p>
<p>9 MONTHS</p>
<p>Total revenue			  12,418,951	12,233,243</p>
<p>Operating (Loss)		     (6,398,311)     (2,542,003)</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss)		    (6,056,095)	  788,766</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss) Per Share		 (0.76)	    (0.10)</p>
<p>NOTES: Current year results include a $605,000 or $0.08 writedown on of the company's China Development Program.</p>
<p>The prior year's results include a gain on the sale of securities of $312,000 or $0.04 per share, for the quarter, and $1.93 million or $0.24 a share for the nine-month period ending March 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Full company name is Ultralife Batteries Inc.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 659-1610))</p>
